# Two Quick Things to Keep in Mind

    Windows Firewall on the Host & VMs: By default, Windows blocks incoming ICMP (ping) requests until File and Printer Sharing is enabled or the firewall rule is allowed. If a ping fails even with matching IPs, check Windows Defender Firewall on the target machine.

    Host DNS (Optional later): Once your Domain Controller (10.0.10.10) is up and running DNS, you can add 10.10.10.1 as the Preferred DNS server on your host's vEthernet (Lab-Internal) adapter if you want to manage the domain from your host PC using RSAT.


